3.1 Preliminaries: SmolVLA
SmolVLA is a lightweight Vision-Language-Action model consisting of two main components: a frozen VLM backbone and a trainable action expert. VLM Backbone.SmolVLA adopts SmolVLM2-500M as its vision-language backbone, comprising a SigLIP vision encoder and a language model. The VLM processes visual observations and language instructions to produce contextual representations. During training, the VLM backbone is frozen to preserve its pre-trained knowledge. Action Expert.The action expert is a small Transformer network that generates robotic actions based on the VLM’s representations. It consists of multiple Transformer layers, each containing a cross-attention module (attending to the VLM’s key-value cache) and a feed-forward network (FFN). The FFN in each layer adopts the SwiGLU architecture:
FFN(x) =W down ·(SiLU(W gate ·x)⊙W up ·x)(1)
whereW gate ∈R dff ×d,W up ∈R dff ×d,W down ∈R d×dff are learnable weight matrices,dis the hidden dimension, andd ff is the intermediate dimension.
