3.4 Shared Expert with Tunable Weight
Inspired by DeepSeek-MoE [6], we introduce a shared expertE s that is always activated for all tokens, providing a stable baseline output. The shared expert has the same SwiGLU architecture as the routed experts but with independent parameters. The final output of the MoE-FFN layer combines the shared expert output and the routed expert output through a tunable weight parameterα:
y(x) =α·E s(x) +y routed(x)(11)
wherey(x)is the final MoE-FFN layer output,E s(x)is the shared expert output,y routed(x)is the aggregated routed expert output defined in Eq. (14), and α∈[0,1]is the shared expert weight that controls the relative contribution of the shared expert. This parameter provides continuous control between two complementary roles:
– Pre-trained capability inheritance(α→1): The shared expert preserves the pre-trained knowledge of the original dense FFN, ensuring training stability. – Expert specialization(α→0): The routed experts gain greater influence, enabling task-specific specialization.
Note that the shared expert is initialized with the exact pre-trained dense FFN weights without added noise, while the routed experts receive noise perturbation (Sect. 3.5). This asymmetric initialization ensures that the shared expert serves as a reliable baseline from the start of training.
