Implementation Details.SmolVLA-MoE is built on top of the SmolVLA architecture. The VLM backbone (SmolVLM2-500M) is frozen during training. The dense FFN layers of the action expert are replaced with MoE-FFN layers through Sparse Upcycling initialization. With 4 routed experts plus 1 shared expert, the total stored parameters of SmolVLA-MoE are∼800M. During inference, only 1 expert FFN is activated per token, resulting in∼100M activated parameters in the action expert module and∼500M total activated parameters including the frozen VLM backbone—identical to the dense baseline SmolVLA. Key hyperparameters include: learning rate 1e-4 with AdamW optimizer, batch size 48, 120,000 training steps with 4,000 warmup steps, load balancing weight λ= 0.01, expert initialization noiseσ= 0.02, and 10 Flow Matching denoising steps. All experiments are conducted on a single NVIDIA RTX 4090 GPU (24GB VRAM). Each configuration is trained for 120,000 steps with the same random seed to ensure fair comparison.
